**[P3] Cache growing-alias fallbacks to prevent exponential memory use**

A short chain of implicit aliases can reuse the same static specialization in both argument slots of a growing recursive alias. The new fallback visits both slots because neither changes during materialization. `TypeTransformerVisit::Cycle` skips cache insertion, so each level doubles the visits to shared descendants. Every visit also appends to `materialization_dependencies`, which retains the duplicates until the enclosing pending visit finishes. A `Top` annotation in an untrusted workspace can therefore exhaust host memory during native language-server diagnostics when the process has no memory limit.

