**[P3] Stop scanning base methods after a reachable wildcard validator**

A reachable `"*"` validator makes every constructor parameter accept `Any`. The previous lookup returned at that point, but this query continues through later bases. If N distinct one-field subclasses inherit the wildcard ahead of a common base with M unshadowed methods, checking their `__init__` signatures now retains N × M Salsa dependencies on `Definition::kind`. In an untrusted workspace where ty resolves Pydantic, that quadratic growth can exhaust the editor host’s memory during diagnostics.

```suggestion
