**[P3] Deduplicate instances while expanding shared type aliases**

`any_over_type_expanding_aliases` guards active cycles but revisits an alias body each time a sibling references it. The previous recursion check discarded those visits. This `push` retains one entry per occurrence, so a compact graph of shared tuple aliases in a generic union parameter can require exponential heap space, even when the parameter has no nested union and the list is never read. During diagnostics in an untrusted workspace, that allocation can exhaust host memory and disrupt the editor. Keeping one entry per distinct type preserves the class lookup order and bounds the collection.

```suggestion
