body:
A subclass can make an inherited field writable and still inherit the frozen base’s covariance. Do we need handling for that?

```python
from pydantic import BaseModel

class Frozen[T](BaseModel, frozen=True):
    value: T

class Thawed[T](Frozen[T], frozen=False):
    pass

def overwrite(box: Thawed[object]):
    box.value = 0

def run(box: Thawed[str]):
    overwrite(box)
    return box.value.upper()
```

Main rejects `overwrite(box)`. In this PR, ty accepts the whole example, so `run(Thawed[str](value="abc"))` reaches `.upper()` on an `int`.

`Thawed` declares no fields of its own, so its invariant default never applies to `value`. The same thing happens if the subclass makes `value` writable by overriding `__setattr__`.

