This recheck also discards a valid specialization for `list(cls)`:

```python
from enum import Enum

class Mode(Enum):
    A = 1

    @classmethod
    def all(cls) -> list["Mode"]:
        return list(cls)
```

The base accepts this. On the PR we infer `list[Self@all]` and report an invalid return. The fresh list can have element type `Mode`, and passing `cls` directly to a parameter of type `Iterable[Mode]` succeeds on both revisions. Ordinary assignability and call-argument checking disagree here. Could we limit the recheck to speculative union narrowing so this direct return keeps its context? This showed up in [Schemathesis](https://github.com/schemathesis/schemathesis/blob/7bb356c55b93b974a123f2cac3b6a5d964210917/src/schemathesis/generation/modes.py#L26).

