body:
This retry can introduce false negatives when the contextual-inference error was correct. If inference from the arguments alone fails to solve a type variable, the retry can produce `Unknown` or a type containing `Unknown`. That can pass the argument and return checks even when the code is invalid. This willingness to retry and fallback to an `Unknown` inference can also trigger `unsound-return` on valid code.

```python
class Counter:
    def __next__(self) -> int:
        return 1

    def text(self) -> str:
        return next(self)

    def read(self) -> int | None:
        return next(self)
```

On this PR, `text` passes the default checks even though it returns `1`. For `read`, the `int` arm already accounts for `next(self)`, but retrying the `None` arm adds `Unknown` and produces a new `unsound-return` warning for `int | Unknown`. (The root cause in this case is an existing gap in constraint collection between typevar upper bounds and generic protocols -- but the retry exposes existing gaps like this in a bunch of new cases.)

The ecosystem run shows both effects.

- A correct argument error disappears in [Ibis](https://github.com/ibis-project/ibis/blob/6d40f963fee940063e09956c7e60d073f4302259/ibis/expr/types/relations.py#L4965) and [Bokeh](https://github.com/bokeh/bokeh/blob/1ad3b4fda2a6c14ded93644ab7adcab9ab458e1c/src/bokeh/server/auth.py#L68) with default narrowing, and in [xarray](https://github.com/pydata/xarray/blob/85b83fe12a52cd103595cf4435afd80fbd027616/xarray/structure/combine.py#L72) and [Scrapy](https://github.com/scrapy/scrapy/blob/e63a574c767d7a9438c21db158f605f1c44c6e6a/scrapy/utils/defer.py#L717) with strict generic narrowing.
- A valid return gains an `unsound-return` warning in [Jinja](https://github.com/pallets/jinja/blob/5ef70112a1ff19c05324ff889dd30405b1002044/src/jinja2/lexer.py#L372) and its vendored copy in [Spack](https://github.com/spack/spack/blob/ab3f3ac5f48d4d636d82bb317e24dd59494f4d32/lib/spack/spack/vendor/jinja2/lexer.py#L370).

Seems like this could maybe be addressed in this PR by refusing the retry if the fallback type is just `Unknown`?

Not sure how concerning this is -- it's mostly false negatives and new `unsound-*` (which aren't enabled by default). The Schemathesis case (commented separately above) seems worse.

