body:
This could be done as follow-up but I noticed that pydantic models generates the `__hash__` method dynamically based on the value of `flag` so any pydanctic models with `frozen=True` is always going to be hashable even if the base class defines the `__hash__` method conditionally. So the following should be accepted but its currently rejected on this PR.

```py
def check(flag: bool) -> None:
    class Parent(BaseModel):
        __eq__ = object.__eq__

        if flag:
            def __hash__(self) -> int:
                return 42

    class Child(Parent, frozen=True):
        __eq__ = object.__eq__

    # emits a diagnostic
    accepts_hashable(Child())
```

Maybe we should only check whether the base class has definitely not defined `__hash__` for frozen pydantic models.

